<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Allgäu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Allgäu is a region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia-bavaria">Bavarian Swabia</a>, with smaller parts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> it was divided among the prince-abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kempten">Kempten</a>, the prince-bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a>, several imperial cities and noble lordships. It is known for dairy farming and cheese.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/allgau.jpg" alt="Allgäu" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Melancholie · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Allg%C3%A4u.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
